<h2>The buyer's shortlisting framework</h2>
<p>Five steps we recommend before signing any premium interior contract in Pune.</p>
<h4>1. Shortlist by category, not by ranking</h4>
<p>Decide whether you want an architect-led studio, a factory-direct turnkey firm or an emerging boutique before comparing portfolios. Comparing across categories is comparing different products.</p>
<h4>2. Visit one completed project per shortlisted firm — ideally two-plus years old</h4>
<p>In Pune, an older project tells you what you most need to know: how the materials aged through monsoons. Look at wardrobe edge banding, hardware silence, veneer joins and any swelling near wet areas.</p>
<h4>3. Demand a room-by-room itemised quote with grade and brand</h4>
<p>Any credible firm names 710 BWP for wet areas, BWR for dry, hardware brands (Blum, Hettich, Hafele), veneer suppliers and stone sources. "Premium plywood, quality hardware" is a placeholder, not a commitment.</p>
<h4>4. Insist on a 3D walkthrough before signing execution</h4>
<p>Modern software makes this trivial. A studio that resists is either understaffed or hoping you'll approve unresolved decisions. Walk the whole home in 3D and confirm every fixed element.</p>
<h4>5. Get warranty terms in writing — with moisture coverage spelled out</h4>
<p>Ask specifically whether the warranty covers moisture-related failures in wet-area plywood and soft-close mechanisms, what voids it, and whether service is direct or via a channel partner. In Pune, this clause is the one that matters most.</p>
<h2>Material specification checklist</h2>
<p>A premium Pune quote at any tier should specify the following. If it doesn't, ask — especially the items marked for humidity.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Plywood (critical for Pune).</strong> 710-grade BWP in kitchens and wet areas, BWR in wardrobes and living. Named brand — CenturyPly, Greenply, Kitply or equivalent.</li>
  <li><strong>Hardware (critical for Pune).</strong> Corrosion-resistant hinges, channels and lift-ups by brand (Blum, Hettich, Hafele), with soft-close and stated load ratings.</li>
  <li><strong>Edge banding &amp; MDF sealing (critical for Pune).</strong> Four-side edge banding, and any MDF fully sealed to block moisture ingress.</li>
  <li><strong>Veneer or laminate.</strong> Engineered veneer thickness (0.5mm+), sheet manufacturer and finishing method (PU matte, PU high gloss). For laminate, brand and grade (1mm+ for shutters).</li>
  <li><strong>Modular kitchen carcass.</strong> Full BWP plywood, edge-banded on all four sides, 18mm minimum.</li>
  <li><strong>Countertops.</strong> Engineered stone (Caesarstone, Silestone, Kalinga Stone) or natural stone — with slab thickness and edge profile.</li>
  <li><strong>False ceiling.</strong> Gypsum board brand (Saint-Gobain, USG Boral), section spacing and finish paint grade.</li>
  <li><strong>Lighting.</strong> Named fixture brands, colour temperature (2700–3000K living, 4000K kitchen task), CRI 90+ for premium, with dimming zones.</li>
  <li><strong>Painting.</strong> Brand and finish grade — for premium expect Asian Paints Royale Luxury, Berger Silk or equivalent, with anti-fungal treatment for external walls.</li>
  <li><strong>Wallpaper.</strong> Named manufacturer, roll dimensions and adhesive spec — moisture-resistant backing where used near wet zones.</li>
</ul>
